{
  "_meta": {
    "locales": "Every translatable value is an object keyed by locale. A locale is NEVER mandatory: getTrad (src/js/modules/utils.js) tries the country key (fr-ca), then the language (fr), then any key starting with it, then en-us, then en — so a market with no copy of its own renders English rather than nothing. Adding a language means adding its key next to en-us; nothing else changes. The one rule is never to leave a key as an empty string: the country key is matched before the fallback runs, so an empty fr-ca renders blank instead of falling through to fr. A locale with no copy yet simply has no key. The keys present here also ARE the locale list the dev prompt offers (tasks/prompt.task.js > localesForVariant).",
    "source": "Copy transcribed from Figma 'SGH - RB META APEROL': desktop 1020:42173, mobile 1020:47170, title 1020:36519. The hideWhenOnlyDifferences flags are the designer's 'Don't show in differences' annotations on that desktop frame.",
    "productCodes": "PLACEHOLDER. productId / upc / pdpUrl below point at two real Ray-Ban Meta products on stage so the module can be seen working end to end; they are NOT the Gen 2 / Gen 3 the copy describes. Swap them when the real codes land — see README, 'The endpoint takes a product id, not a UPC'.",
    "icons": "Icon values are resolved against package.json > projectConfigurations.paths.productionImage (https://media.sunglasshut.com/table-comparison-component/img/ in production, ./static/images/ in dev), so the brand subfolder is part of the value. An absolute http(s) url is used as-is instead — see isSelfContainedUrl in src/js/contents.js."
